# Staging / production connection strings and API hosting config for the Life Kernel.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in your Supabase values, or
# set these variables in your shell / CI instead. `bsk migrate` and
# scripts/migrate-staging.ps1 read BSK_CONNECTION_STRING; the WinForms pilot
# and LifeOs.Api read both owner and reader strings. See
# docs/pilot/supabase-hosting.md and docs/pilot/deploy.md.
#
# Use the SESSION POOLER connection string from the Supabase dashboard: click
# the "Connect" button at the top of the project page, then "Session pooler"
# (port 5432). It is IPv4-friendly and holds the session for the life of the
# connection, so Npgsql prepared statements work. Do NOT use the Transaction
# pooler (port 6543) for migrations — it breaks session state and prepared
# statements.
#
# Note the pooler username form:  <role>.<project-ref>  (e.g. postgres.abcdef...).
# NEVER commit real values. Production secrets live in Fly (`fly secrets set`)
# and in GitHub Environment secrets.

BSK_CONNECTION_STRING=Host=aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres.<project-ref>;Password=<db-password>;SSL Mode=Require;Trust Server Certificate=true

# Read-only role used by the API (and the WinForms pilot) to read the store.
# Reset the bsk_reader password on staging/prod first (see the runbook), then
# put it here. Through the pooler the username is bsk_reader.<project-ref>.
BSK_READER_CONNECTION_STRING=Host=aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=bsk_reader.<project-ref>;Password=<bsk-reader-password>;SSL Mode=Require;Trust Server Certificate=true

# LifeOs.Api — Supabase Auth (Google + allowlist). Nested keys use `__`.
# Locally prefer `dotnet user-secrets --project src/LifeOs.Api` (see web/README).
# The API refuses to start if issuer, audience, JWKS (or JwtSecret), or
# ALLOWED_EMAILS is missing. Do not deploy with authentication disabled.

# Auth__Issuer=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1
# Auth__Audience=authenticated
# Auth__JwksUrl=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
# Auth__JwtSecret=   # optional legacy HS256 fallback; leave empty when using JWKS
# ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@gmail.com
#
# Container / Fly: public SPA values are runtime env (not Docker build-args).
# fly secrets set VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon>
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Same-origin SPA-in-API container: leave CORS empty (production default).
# Local Vite (`npm run dev`) needs the origins in appsettings.Development.json
# or an explicit override:
# Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=http://localhost:5173
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Fly / Azure set PORT; the API listens on it. Local `dotnet run` uses launchSettings (5280).
# PORT=8080
